      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Latitudes"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Latitudes are parallel horizontal lines measuring distance north or south of the Equator (0°).",
        "Longitudes are vertical lines running from the North Pole to the South Pole, measuring distance east or west of the Prime Meridian (0°).",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is based on the 82.5° E longitude meridian, which is 5 hours 30 minutes ahead of GMT.",
        "The Tropic of Cancer (23.5° N) divides India into almost two equal halves and passes through 8 states.",
        "The Prime Meridian passes through Greenwich, London, and serves as the international reference for 0° longitude."
      ],
      "id": "nvvamus"
    },
